Cano — byte-oriented modal terminal editor

Usage
  cano [--config init.lua] [file]
  cano --help

  A file that does not exist yet opens as an empty buffer and is created on
  the first save.

Modes
  Normal   motions, editing, undo/redo, explorer, search and commands
  Insert   byte insertion, indentation and brace autoclose
  Visual   character/line selection, delete, yank and indentation
  Search   wrapped search and s/old/new replacement
  Command  runtime commands and ! shell execution

Global keys
  Ctrl-Q   quit from any mode (refuses if there are unsaved changes)
  Ctrl-S   save and quit (Normal and Insert modes)
  Ctrl-N   toggle explorer in Normal mode (Escape closes it)
  Ctrl-C   acts as Escape in every mode

File commands
  :w       save
  :q       quit if there are no unsaved changes
  :q!      quit and discard unsaved changes
  :wq      save and quit

Configuration
  If present, the default file is ~/.config/cano/init.lua. Cano uses
  built-in defaults when that file is absent, and options the file does not
  set keep those defaults. Calling setup(table) is optional; its argument
  must be a table when called. syntax, auto_indent, relative, indent and
  undo_size retain the documented Boolean compatibility behavior. setup
  returns exit(code[, message]).
